            <ArticleTitle>Laparoscopic removal of a 5-cm subserous pedunculated myoma with small instruments.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>435-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A mobile, subserous, pedunculated myoma was located on the anterior surface of the uterus in a 45-year-old woman. Bipolar coagulation was performed on the pedicle, and the myoma was dissected with an electrical morcellator and removed through the umbilicus. This technique required placement of one 5- to 12-mm cannula in the umbilicus and two 2-mm miniports at the pubic hairline. This technique is easy to perform, and the patient benefits from minimal postoperative pain and excellent cosmetic results.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
